 of tape or something's  bouncing and it's great that you can do  that  but in typically the animations awesome  but the design sucks right and you're  never gonna get hired in the real world  by any good client if you don't have an  eye for something right and like it like  unless I said like that clients hiring  you just to do one task of animating so  I see it a lot like I said I see  different online education being taught  where it's like click this button you  will learn how to be a great animator  but at the same time you put out the  work and you've made something you've  animated it looks great but it looks  great in the animation terms not in it's  not pleasing to the eye okay so if I am  really good at let's say I can rig a  character and I can make a walk cycle  really look good if my character does  not look good or my scene doesn't look  good in the composition is not looking  correct and I don't understand the rule  of thirds and I don't understand color  palettes and I don't understand what  shape is or line bottom line you're not  going to get hired to do motion graphics  to do motion design as a professional  right maybe a client will come along and  say hey you know can you animate this  this artwork that's already done and  that's great and maybe you can animate  it but if you still don't understand why  that artwork looks great what  compositionally about that is working so  well then you're I'm guessing your  animations still gonna suck right  because you don't understand that things  should be flowing certain ways our eye  should be pointed certain ways and that  that relates to animation right because  you understand what good design is so if  you don't understand that you're not  going to get hired to do this work that  that you want to do so bad and you're  always just kind of have it as a hobby  right and that's great if you want to  keep it as a hobby and just kind of play  around that that's great but if you want  to do this professionally and you want  to get paid to do this you need to  understand  what good design is and some of the  rules about it right so my advice to you  is keep honing your animation skills but  at the same time you need to start  understanding what design is and that  doesn't mean that you have to go hire  someone like me and and take a motion  science course or you have to go hire  this guy over here and take his design  course and be a graphic designer you  don't have to do that right now what you  can do right now or some simple steps  those are steps like you could just look  at work that inspires you and for all of  us we're all attracted to different  types of creative motion design and so  you just need to find something that  inspires you and then I want you to take  that piece and I want you to break it  down okay now if this is like a two or  three-minute title sequence don't take  the entire title sequence and break it  down bit by bit just take like 30  seconds of it or 15 seconds of it a part  that really stands out to you and then  study that and study what about that is  speaking to you visually what about that  now if it's you know part of its the  motion and the animation that's great  you know maybe you already understand  what that is but then start looking at  how things move and why they're moving  and what other parts of that that image  or that title sequence or that piece  online is speaking to you is it the  colors and if it is the colors what  about the colors are working so why are  they complementing each other is it is  it the overall shapes of the design of  whatever's in that piece is it is it the  is it repetition that's happening what  about is it texture these are all  elements of great design so what you can  do right now is just take those pieces  break them down study them and and start  to understand why why they work right  what about them works now that's how I  learned  I never went through a traditional art  school I never went through a  traditional art program I can't draw or  the crap but I have I've taken the time  over the years and I've really studied a  lot of great motion design and I  continue to study it to improve my  skills and I continued to study  designers that speak  to me and I learn from what they do and  I bring it into my own style and my own  methods and I'm able to implement a  strong motion design piece because I do  understand design with the motion right  we are motion designers now some of you  will call us motion graphic artists or  motion graphic designers but the word  graphic is in there the word designer is  in there for a reason okay so I just  encourage you to get out there and start  learning parts of motion design the  design side of it because it is going to  make you a better motion designer in the  long run  so hopefully that this helps you out  helps you understand where you need to  go to get better as a motion designer I  invite you to check out motion science  TV we have lots of great courses we have  lots of amazing memberships to help you  become the best motions designer that  you can be until next time I am Cameron  and this is motion science  [Music]

